	abstract = {Phishing is a common cyberthreat that takes advantage of human weaknesses to get private data, such as bank account information, company secrets, and login passwords, without authorization and is driven by the advancements in Artificial Intelligence. In this research, a variety of phishing strategies are examined and categorised according to their technological sophistication, target specificity, and distribution mechanisms. Alongside more sophisticated strategies like spear phishing, clone phishing, and pharming, common techniques like email phishing, smishing (SMS phishing), and vishing (voice phishing) are examined. AI-generated phishing attempts are also covered in the article. Emerging trends like the deployment of deepfakes, social media manipulation. A comparison of each technique's efficacy and detection difficulties reveals how phishing threats are constantly changing. The article concludes by going over current countermeasures, such as user education, sophisticated detection tools, incorporation of Artificial Intelligence in existing methods and adaptive frameworks for cybersecurity, highlighting the necessity of a multifaceted strategy to reduce these risks. This article offers a thorough grasp of phishing tactics and guides the creation of strong defences by combining current research with real-world case studies. © 2025 IEEE.},
